    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link AccountingChronology#isLeapYear(long)} for an accounting calendar that places its leap week in month 13. <p>In this calendar a leap year is one that contains the extra leap week, so {@code isLeapYear} must return {@code true} only for those specific years and {@code false} for every other year. The cases below check a contiguous run of proleptic years around zero so both the leap and non-leap outcomes are covered."
